## Edit D: Add project packages to `local.conf`

Files:

- `/media/abso/yocto/scarthgap/rpi/conf/local.conf`
- `/media/abso/yocto/scarthgap/rpi5/conf/local.conf`

Add:

```conf
IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " traffic-ai-model traffic-robot-app"
```

This makes the AI service and dashboard part of the final image.

---

## Edit E: Align the RPi5 package list with the RPi4 image

File:

- `/media/abso/yocto/scarthgap/rpi5/conf/local.conf`

Add these lines if you want RPi5 to have the same connectivity and development features as RPi4:

```conf
DISTRO_FEATURES:append = " connman"
PACKAGECONFIG:append:pn-connman = " wifi bluetooth"

IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " \
    git \
    teleop-twist-keyboard \
    wpa-supplicant \
    bluez5 \
    linux-firmware \
    pkgconfig \
    gdb \
"

RPI_EXTRA_CONFIG:append = "\
dtoverlay=pwm-2chan\n\
dtparam=audio=off\n\
"
```

If you do not need PWM or audio changes on RPi5, the `RPI_EXTRA_CONFIG` block can be skipped.

---

## Edit F: Optional cleanup of the network stack

Files:

- `/media/abso/yocto/scarthgap/rpi/conf/local.conf`
- `/media/abso/yocto/scarthgap/rpi5/conf/local.conf`

You must choose one of these approaches:

### Option 1: Keep both `connman` and `networkmanager`

Use this if you already depend on both in your workflow.

Action:

- keep the current package list
- verify on target that only the intended service controls each interface

### Option 2: Use only `connman`

Remove:

```conf
IMAGE_INSTALL += "networkmanager networkmanager-nmcli"
IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " networkmanager-openconnect"
```

### Option 3: Use only `networkmanager`

Remove:

```conf
DISTRO_FEATURES:append = " connman"
PACKAGECONFIG:append:pn-connman = " wifi bluetooth"
IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " \
    connman \
    connman-tools \
    connman-client \
    connman-gnome \
    connman-plugin-wifi \
    connman-plugin-ethernet \
    connman-conf \
"
```

