## 4. Validation Checklist On Target

- boot reaches Linux correctly through U-Boot
- `uname -a` shows the expected Raspberry Pi kernel
- `ls /dev/i2c-*` shows I2C devices if enabled
- `lsmod | rg "i2c|spi"` shows expected modules
- PWM overlay is active if required
- network comes up correctly
- ROS 2 base tools are present
- `traffic-ai-model` command exists
- `traffic-robot-app` command exists
- Qt dashboard starts without missing QML module errors

---

## 5. Recommended Order

1. Fix `rpi-extra.conf`
2. Add `meta-qt6` and both project `meta-tr` layers to `bblayers.conf`
3. Add `traffic-ai-model` and `traffic-robot-app` to `IMAGE_INSTALL`
4. Align the RPi5 package list with RPi4 if needed
5. Decide whether to keep both `connman` and `networkmanager`
6. Build RPi4
7. Build RPi5
8. Validate on target hardware
